{"time": "2026-06-08T23:02:50", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g003_a03_14f1725b_001", "post_id": "iv91ivg", "subreddit": "GlobalTalk", "content": "Is anyone actually tracking where these 'imminent breakthrough' rumors start? Every three days we get a massive headline about a potential deal or a sudden shift in negotiations, always citing the same vague 'official close to the matter.' Then, twelve hours later, both sides release statements that completely contradict the leak. It feels like lazy reporting designed to keep people glued to live feeds."}
