{"time": "2026-06-08T23:03:14", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g003_a03_14f1725b_006", "post_id": "gvrfomo", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "anyone else feel like all these 'imminent deal' headlines are just completely made up? one hour it's a massive breakthrough, the next they aren't even talking. who actually leaks this stuff?"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:03:48", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g003_a03_14f1725b_003", "post_id": "fovy7u9", "subreddit": "news", "content": "It feels like we've traded actual governance for a permanent campaign cycle. Nobody is trying to solve problems; they're just trying to get booked on prime-time cable news. I'd happily vote for the most boring, uncharismatic bureaucrat on the ballot if it meant they just sat at their desk and did the actual work of keeping the country running."}
